  <h2>Why This Matters More Than You Might Think</h2>
  <p>When a house fills with clutter, most sellers are stuck. Traditional real estate agents won't take the listing. Banks won't lend to a buyer. You can't put it on the market without overwhelming cleanup that feels impossible. So you sit with it. The stress builds. Sometimes it affects your health, your relationships, your ability to move forward with your life.</p>
  <p>That's where I come in. I don't need you to touch a single box. The house sells as-is. You get the proceeds. You're done.</p>

  <h2>What Happens to Everything Inside</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We secure the property and manage the interior safely</li>
    <li>Professional hauling and disposal of items</li>
    <li>Anything valuable gets identified and handled appropriately</li>
    <li>The house is cleared, cleaned, and prepared for resale or renovation</li>
    <li>You never have to step foot back inside if you don't want to</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The Honest Trade-Off</h2>
  <p>A cash offer will typically be below full retail market value — that's the trade-off for speed, certainty, and zero prep costs. But when you factor in the cost of a dumpster service (often $1,500-$5,000+), the time and stress of sorting, the risk a traditional sale falls through during inspection, and the agent commissions (5-6%) — a fair cash offer often puts more money in your pocket with way less pain.</p>
  <p>We'll always give you a straight answer about what the number is and why.</p>

